# Foundry

[![C++](https://img.shields.io/badge/Language-C%2B%2B-00599C?style=flat&logo=cplusplus&logoColor=white)](https://isocpp.org/)
![Platform Windows](https://img.shields.io/badge/Platform-Windows-0078D6?style=flat&logo=windows&logoColor=white)
![Platform Linux](https://img.shields.io/badge/Platform-Linux-2d2d2d?style=flat&logo=linux&logoColor=white)
![Platform macOS](https://img.shields.io/badge/Platform-macOS-000000?style=flat&logo=apple&logoColor=white)
![License](https://img.shields.io/github/license/DMsuDev/foundry?style=flat&label=License&logo=open-source-initiative&logoColor=white)

**Foundry** is a cross-platform C++ utility library providing a collection of general-purpose tools for developers.

Built with **C++17** as its baseline standard, it targets **Linux, macOS, and Windows** with a focus on simple, reusable APIs.

## 🚧 Project Status

> [!WARNING]
> Foundry is currently in **WIP development**. The public API is not yet considered stable and may change between releases.

Until the first stable release, consumers should pin Foundry to a specific release tag or commit rather than tracking the development branch.

The current version is defined in the root [`VERSION`](VERSION) file.

